# harness-maker Workflow Rules (Cursor)

This project uses a harness generated by [harness-maker](https://github.com/noel/harness-maker).
Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.md`; Cursor reads this `.mdc` file with `alwaysApply: true`,
injecting it into every conversation as ambient context.

> **Minimum supported Cursor**: 2.4 (2026-01-22 — first to bundle subagents,
> skills, and Claude Code hooks compatibility).
> **Recommended**: 3.2+ (2026-04-24 — agent-first redesign, native worktrees,
> `/best-of-n`).

## LLM-first design (highest priority)

Use the model's judgment instead of rule-based branching wherever possible.

- Ambiguity detection, interview follow-up questions, extraction, summarization,
  and convergence checks are all delegated to the model.
- Slash commands are written so that the model directly judges, extracts, and
  generates output — Python is the type-contract / persistence / safety layer.

## Agent dispatch — single source `.claude/agents/`

Reviewer agents live at `.claude/agents/<name>.md`. Cursor reads this directory
natively (Cursor 2.4+ subagents compatibility with `.claude/agents/`).

Default reviewer set: `code-reviewer`, `security-reviewer`, `performance-reviewer`,
`ux-reviewer`, `concurrency-reviewer`, `consensus-arbiter`, `executor`,
`autoloop-coder`. The preset (Side / Production) determines which reviewers are
enabled by default.

## Slash commands — single source `.claude/commands/hm/`

`/hm:<name>` slash commands live at `.claude/commands/hm/<name>.md`. Cursor 2.4+
reads this location natively (verified empirically via kairos 0.5.7 forensic on
2026-05-08 — `tests/cursor-compat/results-2026-05-08.md`). No `.cursor/commands/`
mirror is required.

Representative commands:

- `/hm:research`, `/hm:plan`, `/hm:execute`, `/hm:review`, `/hm:wrapup`, `/hm:verify`
- `/hm:loop` — bounded autoloop runner
- `/hm:refresh` — anti-rot crawl + stale-asset scan
- `/hm:ai-readiness` — 3-layer readiness audit

## Atomic stages

Seven atomic stages compose into named workflows:

- `research` / `spec` / `plan` / `execute` / `review` / `wrapup` / `verify`
- A user-named "fused" workflow is a stage sequence run from a single command
- Every phase auto-commits at the end (handled by the autoloop wrapup stage)

## Permissions

- **Reviewer agents** — read-only (`Read`, `Grep`, `Bash(git diff:*)`,
  `Bash(git log:*)`). `Write` / `Edit` and external commands (curl, npm, rm)
  are denied.
- **Executor agent** — write allowed only inside `.worktrees/**`. Dangerous
  commands (`curl * | sh`, `eval *`, `Write(/etc/**)`, `Write(~/.ssh/**)`)
  are denied.
- All harness-generated files carry frontmatter with `generated_by`,
  `content_hash`, `source_template`, and `harness_maker_version`. Cursor-only
  assets (`.cursor/rules/*.mdc`, `.cursor/mcp.json`) omit these to avoid
  parser strict-reject; sidecar metadata may be introduced in Phase 2.4 if
  reconcile-by-hash becomes necessary for `.cursor/` files.

## Worktrees

`.worktrees/` (gitignored). Both Claude Code's worktree-isolator and Cursor
3.0+ `/worktree` share this directory — cleanup is prefix-matched so each
side touches only its own (`phase-*`, `autoloop-*` for harness-maker).

### `/best-of-n` interop (Cursor 3.0+)

Cursor 3.x ships native `/best-of-n` for parallel agent runs. It uses
`.worktrees/` with its own naming convention. Because harness-maker reserves
the `phase-*` and `autoloop-*` prefixes for its own cleanup, the two systems
coexist safely — `/best-of-n` will neither stomp nor be stomped by harness
worktrees. Use both freely.

## Security gates

**Hook schemas diverge by IDE** — this is intentional, not a bug:

- `.claude/hooks/hooks.json` (Claude Code) — PascalCase keys + nested
  `{matcher, hooks:[{type, command}]}` shape
- `.cursor/hooks.json` (Cursor IDE) — lowercase camelCase keys + flat
  `{matcher, command}` shape + `version: 1`

Each IDE reads only its own dedicated file. Verified empirically via kairos
0.5.7 forensic 2026-05-08 (see `tests/cursor-compat/results-2026-05-08.md`).
Both files wire PreToolUse / PostToolUse / Stop / PreCompact hooks for the
same five gates: secrets leak, permission drift, hook injection, CVE scan,
prompt injection. The hook commands run via `uv run --with <pkg> python -m
harness_maker.gates.X`.

## Models

Default recommendation: `claude-opus-4-7` (`harness.yaml.default_model`).
Per-agent overrides go in `harness.yaml.agent_models` (see ADR-002 +
docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md > Agent Models). Cursor users may override freely, but
prompts contain Claude-specific patterns (`<thinking>` blocks, role framing)
so quality may degrade on other models.

## Memory

- `.claude/memory/failures.md` — failure cases learned by the autoloop
  (user-appendable)
- `.claude/memory/wiki.md` — domain notes added by the user
- `.claude/memory/session/` — per-session progress snapshots

## Anti-rot

`/hm:refresh` crawls four sources (Anthropic blog, GitHub releases, arxiv,
OSV.dev), checks for stale domain packs, and runs a version-drift check.
Nothing is auto-applied — the user confirms each proposed change.

